{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773166010,"nonce":"HKu9aK+I7tK6YtfzZELFGsbeq10=","title":"PenzaiSubgraph should be is_composite=False (opaque leaf, not a feedbax-graph composite)","message":"PenzaiSubgraph wraps an externally-defined Penzai model identified by builder_name. Its internals are Penzai primitives (not feedbax components), so entering it shows an empty canvas that has no relation to what it actually computes. This is misleading.\n\nFix: set is_composite=False in the registry. PenzaiSubgraph is an opaque leaf from the Studio graph perspective. If Penzai model inspection is ever desired, it requires a Penzai-native viewer, not the feedbax subgraph editor.","files":null}]}